cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the released models, please cite the manuscript and the upstream CycleGAN/pix2pix software."
title: "AxialFlowNet: geometry-driven image translation for serial sectioning microscopy"
abstract: >-
  AxialFlowNet is a geometric flow-field generator: a shared ResNet backbone
  feeds a flow branch that predicts a 2-D displacement field used to warp the
  input image, and a bounded texture-residual branch that supplies a pixel-level
  correction. Training combines the adversarial and cycle-consistency losses
  with an axial-monotonicity penalty, an SSIM/Sobel structural loss and
  total-variation, monotonicity and magnitude regularisation of the predicted
  flow field. This package additionally contains the paired mitochondrial
  experiments and the axial multi-scale discriminator.
authors:
  - family-names: "Wu"
    given-names: "An"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/Michalehe/AxialFlowNet"
keywords:
  - image-to-image translation
  - optical flow
  - de-stretching
  - serial sectioning microscopy
